This repository is a release snapshot of a Lean 4 formalization of the answers to Problem 27 of the
Open Quantum Problems list, from the PSI paper "CGLMP optimality and the strength of Bell tests". The
Lean files under CGLMPBounds/ are taken from PSI's development repository (the import cone of the
theorems in Challenge.lean), with the Lean module-system header added, the changes the module system
requires (four definitions made public, three Mathlib imports added, two proofs that unfolded
non-exposed Mathlib definitions rewritten with Mathlib's public lemmas), one hypothesis renamed
(hC6), and comment edits. The axiom pin CGLMPBounds/Audit/FinalCheck.lean was written for this
release.

Comparator checks that the theorems proved in
Solution.lean are exactly the statements in Challenge.lean, using only the three standard axioms, and
the proofs are replayed by Lean's kernel and by independent kernels.

Provenance and use of AI. This result was released by Physical Superintelligence (PSI). The
mathematics was developed by PSI researchers working with AI models (OpenAI's GPT-6-Astra and
Anthropic's Claude Fable 5.1) in automated research workflows at PSI. The Lean formalization was
written by AI agents (Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code, and OpenAI's GPT-6-Astra in Codex) under PSI's direction. David Turturean and Ning Bao
are responsible for the correctness of the paper. The paper's AI disclosure has the details;
formalization.yaml records which agent did which part.

